# SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000193  -  CAT II
# The web server must disable HTTP/1.x downgrading.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000193
group:           V-264363
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-002418
control_rev5:    SC-8

contribution:    Splunk has no HTTP version downgrade setting, so its only bearing is that
                 web.conf [expose:<unique_name>] allowRemoteProxy and the deprecated
                 remoteProxyLegacyRequireDoubleEncodedUriArgs remain at their default of
                 false, leaving no legacy URI argument rewriting path enabled.

external:        The reverse proxy or load balancer that terminates HTTP/2 and performs any
                 downgrade, which must disable HTTP/1.x downgrading or validate the
                 rewritten request against the HTTP/1.1 specification
external:        The organizational determination that HTTP downgrading is operationally
                 necessary, which the check text makes a CAT III finding rather than a
                 configuration setting

manual_reason:   Splunk Web and the splunkd REST server serve HTTP/1.1 only, so no HTTP/2
                 request is ever rewritten to HTTP/1.x inside the application and no
                 setting governs that rewrite or the validation of a rewritten request; the
                 settings the check inventory maps here replay REST calls between search
                 head cluster members (server.conf [shclustering] sid_proxying,
                 ss_proxying, ra_proxying and alert_proxying are marked internal or expert
                 use at server.conf.spec:4847-4877, restmap.conf [restreplayshc] lists
                 replay methods and node strategies at restmap.conf.spec:465-485, and
                 web.conf [expose:<unique_name>] allowRemoteProxy governs the remote-proxy
                 endpoint at web.conf.spec:1545-1568), none of which selects an HTTP
                 version.

citation:        SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000193 check and fix text; web.conf.spec:1129-1142,
                 1545-1568; server.conf.spec:4847-4877; restmap.conf.spec:465-485
finding:         This requirement cannot be decided from Splunk configuration; the HTTP/2
                 terminator in front of Splunk Web must be shown either to disable HTTP/1.x
                 downgrading or to reject rewritten requests containing new lines in
                 headers, colons in header names or spaces in the request method.
